@startuml Buy Goods - Use Case Diagram

!define ACTOR_COLOR #FFE6E6
!define SYSTEM_COLOR #E6F3FF
!define USECASE_COLOR #FFF9E6

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam actor {
    BackgroundColor ACTOR_COLOR
    BorderColor #CC0000
}
skinparam usecase {
    BackgroundColor USECASE_COLOR
    BorderColor #FF9900
}
skinparam rectangle {
    BackgroundColor SYSTEM_COLOR
    BorderColor #0066CC
}

actor Buyer as buyer
actor "Credit Card Company" as cc_company
actor "Bank" as bank
actor "Shipping Service" as shipping

rectangle "Company System" {
    usecase "Buy Goods" as buy_goods
    usecase "Create Order" as create_order
    usecase "Take Payment by Credit Card" as take_payment
    usecase "Handle Returned Goods" as handle_returns
    usecase "Check Inventory\n(IBM OS/390)" as check_inventory
    usecase "Ship Order" as ship_order
    usecase "Send Invoice" as send_invoice
    usecase "Process Payment" as process_payment
}

buyer --> buy_goods : initiates
buy_goods --> create_order : includes
buy_goods --> check_inventory : includes
buy_goods --> ship_order : includes
buy_goods --> send_invoice : includes
buy_goods --> process_payment : includes
buy_goods --> take_payment : extends
buy_goods --> handle_returns : extends

take_payment --> cc_company : uses
process_payment --> cc_company : uses
process_payment --> bank : uses
ship_order --> shipping : uses
handle_returns --> buyer : notifies

note right of buy_goods
  **Main Success Scenario (11 steps):**
  1. Buyer calls with purchase request
  2. Capture buyer details & goods
  3. Check inventory (IBM OS/390)
  4. Provide goods info & pricing
  5. Buyer confirms order
  6. Create order in system
  7. Ship order
  8. Ship invoice
  9. Buyer receives & verifies
  10. Buyer pays invoice
  11. Record payment
  
  **Extensions (8 alternative flows):**
  - 3a: Out of stock items
  - 4a: Expedited shipping
  - 5a: Direct credit card payment
  - 7a: Shipping unavailable
  - 8a: Invoice delivery fails
  - 10a: Buyer returns goods
  - 10b: Buyer disputes charge
  - 10c: Payment fails
  
  **Sub-Variations (4 steps with alternatives):**
  - Step 1: 4 contact methods
  - Step 2: 3 capture methods
  - Step 7: 4 shipping methods
  - Step 10: 6 payment methods
end note

@enduml
